{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1540456400,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzMjk2MjU4Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2947#issuecomment-432962583"},"message":"I'm not sure what you mean by \"not `datalad run` aware. `run-procedure` does call `run` and therefore creates a record.","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1540456400,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDE0NDM0Mzc2Mw=="},"target":"12d1e090be3392aa2b2ecd6f6a6c8da359e2d8b8e8b7f790beabe6b62efb8c63","message":"I'm not sure what you mean by \"not `datalad run` aware\". `run-procedure` does call `run` and therefore creates a record.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1540470465,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzMzAzMDg3MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2947#issuecomment-433030870"},"message":"\u003e `run-procedure` does call `run` and therefore creates a record.\n\n`run-procedure` calls `run` with `explicit=True` and `outputs=None`, so no commit is created.  This use of `run` was prompted/motivated by gh-2593:\n\n\u003e  extend the run API to support all the running aspects without the result capture (i.e. a mere frontend for the Runner class)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1540471737,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzMzAzNzI5NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2947#issuecomment-433037295"},"message":"Ah, right. Stupid me used procedures, that call `run` themselves (and therefore got a record).","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1540473069,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzMzA0NDIzMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2947#issuecomment-433044233"},"message":"However, I'm not yet sure how to approach this. Of course we can simply forward `inputs`, `outputs` and `explicit`, but in general procedures are supposed to be usable with no further knowledge about those internal details. Furthermore, the ones we already use are leaving the dataset clean. They would do whatever they need to know and call datalad commands (including `run`) themselves. In effect there would be nothing to commit with `run`'s current approach. In order to say \"This is what the procedures was doing\", `run-procedure` would need to build a record based on the squashed commits of the procedure (or sth similar). This in turn could destroy what the procedure tried to provide by its commits.\n\nI guess it boils down to: What would a `rerun-procedure` do and what kind of record is required to do so?","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1540473069,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDE0NDQ0NzEzNQ=="},"target":"b36bc8f988a67b23f07fc8011c6491d268072b9ae41693f444e06fce142fc7d9","message":"However, I'm not yet sure how to approach this. Of course we can simply forward `inputs`, `outputs` and `explicit`, but in general procedures are supposed to be usable with no further knowledge about those internal details. Furthermore, the ones we already use are leaving the dataset clean. They would do whatever they need to do and call datalad commands (including `run`) themselves. In effect there would be nothing to commit with `run`'s current approach. In order to say \"This is what the procedures was doing\", `run-procedure` would need to build a record based on the squashed commits of the procedure (or sth similar). This in turn could destroy what the procedure tried to provide by its commits.\n\nI guess it boils down to: What would a `rerun-procedure` do and what kind of record is required to do so?","files":null}]}